type: software
title: "Can AI Recognize Itself? Why self-related indicators cannot settle machine consciousness, and what a tenth-century Kashmiri debate anticipated: code and results"
authors:
  - given-names: Ajay
    family-names: Hagan
    affiliation: Spanda Research
version: 1.0.0
# No doi field yet: Zenodo mints this repository's DOI when v1.0.0 is released.
# Add it here (and to README.md) after the release.
# date-released: YYYY-MM-DD   (set on release)
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/yoddha2248/Can-AI-Recognize-Itself"
abstract: >-
  Code and results for the paper "Can AI Recognize Itself?". A test ladder of self-related
  indicators (V1, V3, V4a-V4c) on a 21-oscillator self-model, the same questions put to
  GPT-2 Medium (B1, B2, J1), and pre-registered negative controls (a scrambled-weights copy
  and a non-linguistic network). For every test the cheapest cheat and an outside observer
  are built and run. Successor to "Why AI Might Be Conscious — and Why No Test Can Yet Tell"
  (v0.1.0).
keywords:
  - machine consciousness
  - self-models
  - consciousness indicators
  - privileged access
  - negative controls
  - Pratyabhijna
